      "name": "BUBS",
      "year": "1992",
      "type": "Foam & jelly candy",
      "maker": "BUBS (owned by Orkla since 2023)",
      "about": "BUBS began in 1992 in Huskvarna, near Jönköping. The Lindström family put their house up as security for a bank loan to buy their first candy machine. The name comes from four of them: Bernt, Ulrik, Birgitta and Stefan. They chose bold shapes such as skulls, ovals and diamonds. There are many skulls, from sour to salty licorice to Cool Cola. In 2023 the family sold BUBS to Orkla. In 2024 TikTok videos made this candy popular in the U.S. and ever since there has been a lot of interest in Swedish Candy and stores popping up all over New York, LA, and now SF.",
